      Since every fiber $X_{s}$ has an initial object, the map $p|X'$ has the right lifting property with respect to the inclusion $\emptyset \subseteq \Delta ^0$. If $n > 0$, then Lemma <a href="/tag/2FEF7F" data-tag="2FEF7F">2.4.4.8</a> shows that $p|X'$ has the right lifting property with respect to $\bd \Delta ^ n \subseteq \Delta ^ n$. This proves $(1)$. In particular, we deduce that there exists a map $q: S \rightarrow X'$ which is a section of $p$. In view of the uniqueness of initial objects, $(2)$ will follow if we can show that $q$ is an initial object of $\calC $. Unwinding the definitions, we must show that for $n > 0$, any lifting problem 
